        {
          "unit_id": "shift_work",
          "title": "Priya's Shifts",
          "description": "Rutinas de otras personas: present simple con he/she y adverbios de frecuencia. Y a / an o the: a nurse, the hospital.",
          "lessons": [
            {
              "lesson_id": "shift_work_lesson",
              "title": "Present simple: he, she + frequency",
              "steps": [
                {
                  "phase": "context",
                  "type": "audio_context",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "Priya's shifts",
                    "dialogue": [
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Good morning, Priya! You're up early!"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Priya",
                        "text": "I always get up at half past five. I work at the hospital today."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Do you work every day?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Priya",
                        "text": "No. I usually work four days a week. Sometimes I work at night."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "At night? That's hard."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Priya",
                        "text": "Yes, it is. When I work at night, I sleep in the day."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "And Sam? Does he get up early?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Priya",
                        "text": "Sam? Never! He never gets up before ten. He works at the pub, and he finishes at midnight."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Does he work at the pub every day?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Priya",
                        "text": "No, he doesn't. He works there on Thursdays, Fridays and Saturdays. He often plays with his band on Fridays."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "And what does he do on Mondays?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Priya",
                        "text": "He sleeps!"
                      }
                    ],
                    "passage": "It's six o'clock in the morning. Lucía is awake, and there's a light in the kitchen. Priya is there with a cup of tea."
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "discovery",
                  "type": "multiple_choice",
                  "content": {
                    "instructions": "Fíjate en el diálogo y responde.",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "question": "\"He never gets up before ten.\" With he/she, the verb…",
                        "options": [
                          "adds -s",
                          "doesn't change",
                          "adds -ing"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "\"Does he work every day?\" — \"No, he ___.\"",
                        "options": [
                          "doesn't",
                          "don't",
                          "isn't"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "\"I always get up at half past five.\" Always goes…",
                        "options": [
                          "before the verb",
                          "after the verb",
                          "at the end"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "When does Sam work at the pub?",
                        "options": [
                          "Thursdays, Fridays and Saturdays",
                          "every day",
                          "on Mondays"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "Present simple: he, she, it + adverbs of frequency",
                    "explanation": "Con he, she e it el verbo lleva -s: she works, he sleeps. Algunos llevan -es (goes, does, watches, finishes) y los que acaban en consonante + y cambian a -ies (study → studies). Have es irregular: has.\n\nNegativa y pregunta con does / doesn't, y el verbo vuelve a su forma base: He doesn't work on Mondays. Does he get up early? (nunca «Does he gets»).\n\nLos adverbios de frecuencia van antes del verbo principal pero después de be: She always gets up early. Sam is never early.",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Adverbio",
                        "Frecuencia",
                        "Ejemplo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "always",
                          "100%",
                          "Priya always gets up at half past five."
                        ],
                        [
                          "usually",
                          "80%",
                          "She usually works four days a week."
                        ],
                        [
                          "often",
                          "60%",
                          "Sam often plays on Fridays."
                        ],
                        [
                          "sometimes",
                          "40%",
                          "Priya sometimes works at night."
                        ],
                        [
                          "never",
                          "0%",
                          "Sam never gets up before ten."
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "Priya works at the hospital.",
                      "Sam doesn't work on Mondays.",
                      "Does Sam get up early? — No, he doesn't.",
                      "He finishes at midnight."
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "Articles: a / an or the",
                    "explanation": "A / an (un, una) presenta algo por primera vez o dice qué es alguien: She's a nurse. There's a new pub in Clifton.\n\nThe (el, la, los, las) habla de algo concreto que ya conocemos, porque ya lo hemos dicho o porque solo hay uno: There's a new pub. The pub is great. Priya works at the hospital (el hospital de siempre).\n\nSin artículo: con las profesiones en plural y con cosas en general: Nurses work at night. I love music. Y en expresiones como at home, at work, by bus, on Monday, at night.\n\nOjo: en español decimos «es enfermera», pero en inglés las profesiones llevan a / an: She's a nurse, He's an engineer.",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "",
                        "Ejemplo",
                        "Por qué"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "a / an",
                          "Sam is a musician.",
                          "profesión, primera mención"
                        ],
                        [
                          "the",
                          "He works at the pub.",
                          "un sitio concreto que conocemos"
                        ],
                        [
                          "a → the",
                          "I've got a cat. The cat is black.",
                          "primero a, después the"
                        ],
                        [
                          "sin artículo",
                          "I go to work by bus.",
                          "expresiones fijas"
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "Priya is a nurse. She works at the hospital.",
                      "There's a café near our house. The café opens at seven.",
                      "Sam sleeps in the day and works at night.",
                      "I love music, but I don't like the music in this pub."
                    ]
                  }
                },
